module bindings.php.psr7_server_params_input;

// PSR-7's ServerRequestInterface::getServerParams() returns the server
// parameters of the current request -- the object-shaped mirror of the
// $_SERVER superglobal, which the php.input bindings already label key by
// key. The generated package binding for the interface is dependency-gated
// and PHP dependency resolution reads composer.lock, so an application that
// ships composer.json alone (the framework itself, or any project that does
// not commit its lock file) gets no label on the one accessor its request
// object offers. This binding is ungated for the same reason the $_SERVER
// reads are: the method is part of the interface contract, not of a
// particular package's implementation of it.
//
// The label sits on the call result, so every key read out of the returned
// array carries -- including the keys a server sets itself (SCRIPT_NAME).
// That is the same judgement the superglobal bindings already make for
// $_SERVER's request-derived keys, applied one hop later, and it is the
// reason the escape-at-the-write control, not key selection, is what
// separates a rendered prefix from an escaped one.
binding httpInputGetServerParams {
  query pattern callExpr where callee.method == "getServerParams"
  emit source code.HttpInput at call.result
}
